      "writtenOn": "2024-04-11T06:51:08Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "I see what you did, but I\u0027d prefer we don\u0027t require annotating with presubmit. By default, I think we would prefer running these tests in the presubmit. There is no reason for needing to annotate every test class with @presubmit. When a new class is added, it is easy to miss this annotation and not have the test run as part of the presubmit. Instead, using @FlakyTest annotation (including a reason/bug for why) to exclude tests would be a lot more clearer to understand the status when someone is looking at these tests.",
      "parentUuid": "2dc9dd95_80462c9e",
